      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What is Semantic MediaWiki, what can it do for me, and why is it not on Wikipedia yet?&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Semantic MediaWiki (SMW) is a free, open-source extension to MediaWiki – the wiki software that powers Wikipedia – that lets you store and query data within the wiki&amp;#39;s pages.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Semantic MediaWiki is also a full-fledged framework, in conjunction with many spinoff extensions, that can turn a wiki into a powerful and flexible “collaborative database”. All data created within SMW can easily be published via the Semantic Web, allowing other systems to use this data seamlessly.&lt;/p&gt;      </description>
